quran[10]{c,v,t}:
  42,1,"Ha-Mim,"
  42,2,"‘Ayn, Sin, Qaf."
  42,3,"Thus has He revealed to you and those before you, Allah, the All-Mighty, the All-Wise."
  42,4,"To Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. And He is the All-Exalted, the All-Supreme."
  42,5,"The heavens are almost breaking apart over them (in His reverence), while the angels glorify their Lord’s praise (all the time) and seek forgiveness for those on the earth. Behold! Allah is indeed the Most-Forgiving, the All-Merciful."
  42,6,"As for those who take protectors besides Him, Allah is Watchful over them. And (O Prophet,) you are not responsible for them."
  42,7,"Thus, We have revealed a Qur’an in Arabic to you so that you may warn the people of the Mother of the Towns (i.e. the city of Mecca) and those around it. And warn (them) of the Day of Gathering, about which there is no doubt, (when) a group shall be in Paradise, and a group shall be in the Blaze."
  42,8,"Had Allah wished, He could have (easily) made them one community. But He admits whom He pleases into His mercy. And the wrongdoers have no guardian and no helper."
  42,9,Have they taken guardians besides Him? (Say:) ‘It is Allah Who is the Guardian. He gives life to the dead. And He is All-Capable of everything.
  42,10,"Whatever you may differ about, its judgement rests only with Allah. That is Allah, my Lord. In Him do I trust. And to Him, I turn penitently."
